## Why This Is Asked
Autocomplete systems in product search need fast prefix queries with duplicates. A Trie with per-node counts shows practical memory/time trade-offs and handles duplicates transparently.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with endCount and subCount
- Duplicate handling via counts
- O(|word|) insertion/erasure/lookup
- O(|prefix|) prefix query
- Space proportional to total characters stored

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node { constructor(){ this.next = new Map(); this.end=0; this.sub=0; } }
class Trie { constructor(){ this.root=new Node(); }
  insertWord(w){ let cur=this.root; cur.sub++; for(const ch of w){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) cur.next.set(ch,new Node()); cur=cur.next.get(ch); cur.sub++; } cur.end++; }
  eraseWord(w){ let cur=this.root; cur.sub--; for(const ch of w){ cur=cur.next.get(ch); cur.sub--; } cur.end--; }
  containsWord(w){ let cur=this.root; for(const ch of w){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) return false; cur=cur.next.get(ch); } return cur.end>0; }
  countWithPrefix(pref){ let cur=this.root; for(const ch of pref){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) return 0; cur=cur.next.get(ch); } return cur.sub; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What happens if eraseWord called on non-existent word?
- How would you compact memory when many words share prefixes?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a dynamic interval data structure that handles duplicates, supports point-sum queries, and enables k-th weight selection—all without scanning all intervals. It combines segment trees with per-node multisets to achieve range updates and efficient multi-set queries.

## Key Concepts
- Segment tree over coordinate-compressed points for efficient range queries
- Per-node multiset of (weight, id) pairs to handle duplicate intervals
- nodeSum aggregation for fast sum queries at any point
- Binary search over the weight domain combined with order statistics for k-th largest queries

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch for insertInterval/eraseInterval
class IntervalIndex {
  constructor(points) {
    this.tree = new SegmentTree(points.length - 1);
  }

  insertInterval(l, r, w, id) {
    const range = this.getCompressedRange(l, r);
    this.tree.update(range.l, range.r, (node) => {
      node.multiset.add({ weight: w, id });
      node.sum += w;
    });
  }

  eraseInterval(id, w) {
    // Find all intervals containing this id and remove one instance
    this.tree.queryById(id, (node) => {
      node.multiset.delete({ weight: w, id });
      node.sum -= w;
    });
  }

  sumWeightsCoveringPoint(p) {
    const idx = this.compress(p);
    return this.tree.queryPoint(idx, (node) => node.sum);
  }

  kthLargestWeightCoveringPoint(p, k) {
    const idx = this.compress(p);
    const weights = this.tree.getWeightsAt(idx);
    return this.findKthLargest(weights, k);
  }
}
```

